  "stage": {
    "routeId": "camino-norte",
    "index": 6,
    "count": 34,
    "name": "Lezama to Bilbao",
    "theme": "Bilbao",
    "narrative": "A short walking day, and then Bilbao. You enter the city from above — from Mount Avril where the Guggenheim suddenly appears in the valley below, a metallic shape that looks nothing like anything else in your Camino so far. The descent is by stairs. You arrive in the Casco Viejo, the old Gothic quarter, and the rest of the day is yours. Most pilgrims take a rest day. The Guggenheim, Puente Colgante, the Cathedral, the Basílica de Begoña on the hill, tapas in Plaza Nueva — Bilbao deserves more than one night.",
    "closing": "You walked from an oak tree to a Frank Gehry museum in two days. What does the Camino do with that kind of contrast?",
